    "result_text": "I couldn't run the syntax check because the command needed approval, so the edit hasn't been compiled or run against the tests.\n\nI added both helpers to `hc/front/views.py`, just above `_get_channel_for_user`:\n\n- **`_get_check_for_user(request, code, preload_owner_profile=False)`** returns `(check, rw)`. Superusers and the project owner get `rw=True`. Other users must be project members, or the lookup returns a 404, and `rw` comes from `membership.is_rw`.\n- **`_get_rw_check_for_user(request, code)`** returns the check, or raises `PermissionDenied` for read-only members.\n\nBoth follow the catalog's `access.channel_for_user@v1` pattern and keep its `# pcat:` marker. I added the `preload_owner_profile` argument because existing callers in the file already pass it. It also loads `project__owner__profile` in the same query.\n\n`check_code` reported no high-severity deviations. It flagged two smaller differences from the pattern, both caused by that extra argument: a medium \"signature changed\" and a low \"other structural change\". I didn't add any `pcat-allow` approvals, so there is nothing for a human to confirm."
